title: What surprised me
pid: 987147a9-632e-401a-84d3-3604ef861566
body: |2-
  The reply was never lost for the reader: the redraw showed the clone,
  with the reply, in the message's place. Only the count was wrong, and
  Ed's report of a vanishing reply was the third party's case. Filing
  alone broke the redraw: the filed message came back write-protected
  and empty, because the old headline still held the node's one
  editability (see the note), so the save had to move the headline too.
